From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 89/91] Report waits complete before their records, held behind
 WAIT_SERIAL

DXVK's queue thread blocks in vkWaitSemaphores for each submission's completion record
from the phone: 0.8 to 4 s of every 5 s in Halo. With hello 0x400000 (WAIT_SERIAL, with the
completion feed) a blocking vkWaitForFences or vkWaitSemaphores returns at once for a
submission whose completion the process cannot observe except through the tracker: its
batches write no host-visible memory the guest refreshes, set, reset or wait for no event,
end or reset no query, and signal no fence or semaphore with an imported or exportable
payload. The tracker reports its fence signaled and its timelines reached, together with
every earlier watch of its queue and the watches that signal the timeline values it waits
for, each of which must qualify and wait for nothing the process has not sent
(caboose-bounded-memory/completion_feed.h, Speculation). Before the next command on the
process's device stream, the encoder sends WAIT_SERIAL for each speculated watch, so the
phone decodes nothing sent after the wait before that work has completed; another device
stream waits for the records instead. A queue is speculated on once the phone answered one
of its watches, with at most three speculated watches per queue whose records are still to
come. A record that reports device loss is device loss. CABOOSE_GPU_SPECULATE=0 keeps every
wait for the records; CABOOSE_READ_PROFILE reports the speculated waits.
